  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records provide several relevant ingredients but not the later result as a specific design. R2 and R3 show that Cr-containing refractory BCC HEAs can form Cr-rich Laves phases, while R8, R15, R16, and R20 associate multicomponent lattice distortion with dislocation impediment and solid-solution strengthening. R7 supplies the related architectural principle that a continuous ductile BCC matrix containing a suitably distributed intermetallic phase can retain strength while improving ductility, and R18 provides a more distant example of beneficial interconnected or lamellar dual-phase organization. However, none proposes adding a dilute 4.2 at.% Cr concentration to HfMoTaTiZr, predicts the complex Cr2(Ti,Zr,Hf,Ta) reticulated network, or identifies that network as a crack-hindering and plasticity-compensating structure. Thus the literature points in the right direction, but selecting this specific Cr addition and obtaining its beneficial reticulated Laves morphology would require a substantial new design idea."
